{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456490-looking-for-clarification-about-damage-dark-ages-vampire","id":1456490,"title":"Looking for clarification about damage Dark Ages Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-09T19:59:13-07:00","id":1456490,"title":"Looking for clarification about damage Dark Ages Vampire","content":"The information on page 345 of the 25th AE of Dark Ages Vampire seems to contradict itself regarding damage. I know that bashing and lethal damage is soaked with Stamina + Fortitude (if applicable) + armor (if applicable), but what about the claws/teeth of other supernatural creatures? The section on aggravated damage says &quot;only a vampire's Fortitude dots&quot; but in the armor section it says that armor protects against bashing, lethal AND aggravated wounds (excluding fire and sunlight). So which is it? Fortitude dots only or Fortitude + armor (like the text suggests)? Thanks in advance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T21:29:19-07:00","id":1456496,"title":"","content":"It's Fortitude + Armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","ran